WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.870
People often wonder why some entrepreneurs have greater success than others.
人们常常想知道，为什么有些创业者比别人更成功。

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.390
Is it habits, connections, luck, work ethic or some other factor?
是习惯、人脉、运气、敬业精神，还是其他某种因素？

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.630
I believe the key to success is willpower.
我认为成功的关键在于意志力。

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.290
Willpower is the ability to control yourself.
意志力是控制自己的能力。

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.140
It is a strong determination that allows you to do something difficult.
它是一种坚定的决心，能让你去做困难的事情。

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:31.840
It is a behavior we are born with more than one we learn; however, it is possible to not only learn it, but also strengthen it with constant exercise.
它更多是一种与生俱来的行为，而不是后天学会的行为；不过，我们不仅可以学会它，还可以通过不断锻炼来增强它。

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.720
Willpower is just like a muscle; to keep it strong you need to constantly exercise it.
意志力就像肌肉一样；要让它保持强健，你需要不断地锻炼它。

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:44.160
People with a great amount of willpower have the discipline to develop positive, successful habits.
意志力充沛的人有足够的自律来养成积极的、能带来成功的习惯。

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:53.620
Even with an incredible amount of talent, without the discipline and motivation to create positive habits, it can be difficult to achieve success.
即使天赋惊人，如果缺乏养成积极习惯所需的自律和动力，也可能很难取得成功。

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.660
Willpower and habits go hand in hand.
意志力与习惯相辅相成。

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:04.940
It is critical to create good habits and take the actions necessary to stick to those habits day in and day out for greater success.
要取得更大的成功，至关重要的是养成良好的习惯，并采取必要的行动，日复一日地坚持这些习惯。

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:16.430
Almost half of our daily actions are part of our habits and not decisions, so once the correct habits are in place, you will automatically perform those tasks on a day-to-day basis.
我们的日常行为几乎有一半属于习惯，而不是决定，所以一旦正确的习惯确立起来，你每天就会自动完成那些任务。

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:21.310
The best way to create and stick to a habit is to have strong motivation.
养成并坚持一个习惯的最好方法是拥有强烈的动力。

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:31.940
It’s easier to change your habits to lose weight if you have a health issue and you want to be around longer for your kids, or to grow your business if it is something you’re passionate about.
如果你有健康问题，又想为了孩子多活些年，那么改变习惯来减肥就会更容易；如果你热爱自己的事业，那么改变习惯来发展事业也会更容易。

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:38.340
Having a valuable outcome associated with a habit will help you stick to that habit permanently.
让一个习惯与某种有价值的结果联系在一起，会帮助你把这个习惯永久地坚持下去。

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.860
The art of self-control is one that most successful individuals have mastered.
自我控制这门艺术，大多数成功人士都已经掌握了。

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:51.030
Self-control enables you to avoid behaviors that don’t contribute to your success and adopt those that do.
自我控制能让你避免那些无助于成功的行为，并采取那些有助于成功的做法。

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:57.930
Because there is a delayed satisfaction associated with self-control, it can be easy to get off track.
由于与自我控制相伴的满足感要延迟到来，人可能很容易偏离正轨。

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:07.340
However, if you work on sticking to those small positive habits one day at a time, it becomes easier to stay strong and achieve that delayed reward.
不过，如果你努力一天一天地坚持那些小小的积极习惯，保持坚定、获得那份延迟的回报就会变得更容易。

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.900
Once a reward is achieved, it is much easier to continue sticking to your habits.
一旦获得了回报，继续坚持习惯就会容易得多。
